waiver: harness-limit
reason: target_os() is defined per target and a case carries one
  expected.stdout, so it can only be asserted on the legs that compile for
  the same environment. The wasm leg compiles for the CLI world and answers
  "wasi"; the native legs answer "linux", which target_os_linux pins. The
  interpreter answers with its host and is pinned by internal/interp's own
  test. target_os_named asserts on all four backends what every one must
  agree on.
